      "text": "{\"pair_id\": \"Mereret|702380\", \"verdict\": \"different_name\", \"reasoning\": \"The transliteration Mrrwy reads as the signs m, r, r, w, y. In Mereret, M matches m, the first r matches r, and the second r matches the second r. The vowel letters e stand for no sign. The final w and y may be left out in a modern spelling, so they cause no mismatch. However, Mereret ends in a t, and the transliteration has no t at all. The rule only lets a spelling omit an element-final t; it does not let record 1 add one. That t is a leftover consonant that nothing in Mrrwy represents, so the two are different names. Mereret corresponds to Mrrt, the feminine name, while Mrrwy is a different form.\"}"
